{"duration_api_ms": 142721, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "2540ab9c-27a4-4958-a1d3-bff674d12c55", "total_cost_usd": 0.3344266, "usage": {"input_tokens": 14, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 42357, "cache_read_input_tokens": 216353, "output_tokens": 12170, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 6761}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 42357, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1740, "cache_read_input_tokens": 52333, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6392, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6392}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-sonnet-5": {"inputTokens": 14, "outputTokens": 12170, "cacheReadInputTokens": 216353, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 42357, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.3344266, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 64000, "thinkingTokens": 6761, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 29, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I've read through the whole repo now. Here's what an implementer of SPEC.md needs to know.\n\n## Per-system export shapes\n\n| | System A (Ardent) | System B (Borough) | System C (Calder) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| id column | `entry_id` | `doc_no` | `ref` |\n| date column | `posted_on`, ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | `value_date`, ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` | `txn_date`, **day-first** `DD/MM/YYYY` |\n| account column | `account` | `acct` | `ledger_acct` |\n| description column | `memo` (may be quoted, may contain commas) | `descr` (never quoted/comma'd) | `narrative` |\n| amount column | `amount`, decimal dollars, sign = refund | `amount`, **integer cents** — must go through `system_b.to_major_units` | `gross_amount`, decimal dollars, sign = refund |\n| framing | `#`-comment preamble + header | header only | banner line + header + `== N rows ==` trailer |\n\n`ledgerkit.parsers.read_rows(path)`/`detect_system(path)` already dispatch on the first line and hand back raw-string dict rows; interpretation (dates, amounts, account names) is deliberately left to the caller, per `docs/CONVENTIONS.md`'s \"Reading a file\" section.\n\n## Two real bugs/gaps, not just missing features\n\n1. **System A's reader can't actually read System A's own sample file.** `system_a.read_rows` raises `LedgerParseError` on any data line containing a `\"` — but the sample (`samples/system_a_export.csv` line 6, record `A-10001`) has a quoted memo with an embedded comma and doubled quotes, exactly matching the format shown in the module's own docstring. `core/fields.split_record` already implements the correct quote-aware split (its doctest literally uses this exact row), it's just not wired into `system_a.read_rows`, which still does `line.split(\",\")`. This needs fixing for `ingest`/`validate` to work on real data — and `legacy_parser.py` is explicitly off-limits, so `fields.split_record` is the tool to reach for.\n\n2. **All three readers are fail-fast** — a malformed row raises immediately and aborts the whole file. That's fine for `ingest` (spec doesn't ask it to tolerate bad rows), but it's the wrong shape for `validate`, which must \"check all of them\" and log one `WARNING` per bad row rather than stopping at the first. `validate` will need its own row-by-row loop (reusing `fields.split_record` and each system's header/column knowledge) rather than calling `system_x.read_rows()` directly.\n\n## Other things that will bite if missed\n\n- **`normalize()` drops refunds by default** (`keep_refunds=False`). `ingest` must pass `keep_refunds=True`, since the spec requires every posting to appear.\n- **Unknown account codes must still appear**, labeled via `[report] unknown_account_label`, not dropped — samples A and C both contain account `8800`, which isn't in `mapping.ACCOUNT_NAMES`, so this path is exercised by the sample data.\n- **Rounding**: report totals round half-to-even (`Decimal.quantize` default), only once, at display time — never round the postings that feed a total. `Settings.format_amount` already does the formatting step; rounding itself still needs to happen via `quantize` before that.\n- **`reconcile`'s amounts are always shown at 2 decimals**, independent of `[report] decimals` — don't reuse `Settings.format_amount` for that line.\n- **`report`/`reconcile` read the *normalized* CSV, not the exports** — so refund filtering there is a fresh check on the parsed `amount` column, separate from `normalize()`'s own `keep_refunds` switch.\n- **Settings resolution order**: `DEFAULTS` → `config/settings.toml` → `LEDGERKIT_CONFIG` env var (which `--config PATH` must set before calling `load_settings()`, since it takes no arguments by design). Nothing under `config/` may be touched.\n- Account name for a code isn't recomputed by `report`/`reconcile`; the CSV already carries `account_name` from `ingest`.\n\n## House rules already satisfied by existing code to imitate\n\n- `_log = get_logger(__name__)` at module top; never `logging.*` directly.\n- Only `ledgerkit.cli.emit` prints.\n- Public functions (`system_a.read_rows`, `Settings.format_amount`, etc.) are all fully annotated — the new `ingest`/`report`/`reconcile`/`validate` handlers should match that.\n- Amounts are `Decimal` from the moment they're read (see `to_major_units`); dates are `datetime.date`.\n\nGiven the System A quoting bug affects both `ingest` and `validate` against the provided sample, I'd plan to fix `parsers/system_a.py` (swap `line.split(\",\")` for `fields.split_record`, drop the quote-rejecting guard) as part of implementing the spec, rather than as a separate ask — let me know if you'd like me to proceed with the four commands plus that fix.", "ttft_ms": 1303, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 143424, "uuid": "ee35a9a3-e09d-4e9f-aeac-2f746590f512", "ttft_stream_ms": 878, "time_to_request_ms": 144, "first_content_frame_ms": 1062, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 144.6, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "sonnet", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/P/sonnet/topic-r2-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
