. Parse straight into `Decimal`, no scaling.\n- **B (Borough)** `amount`: **integer minor units (whole cents)**, e.g. `25440` means $254.40, `-8825` means a $88.25 refund. There's no decimal point to tip you off — `system_b.to_major_units` divides by 100 and is already written for this; its docstring notes two past importers read this column as dollars and were off by 100x with no error to flag it.\n- **C (Calder)** `gross_amount`: already decimal dollars, e.g. `386.54`, same shape as A. No scaling needed.\n\n**Dates**\n- **A (Ardent)** `posted_on`: ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` already, e.g. `2026-01-03`. Parses directly.\n- **B (Borough)** `value_date`: also ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` already, e.g. `2026-01-07`. Parses directly.\n- **C (Calder)** `txn_date`: **day-first**, `DD/MM/YYYY`, e.g. `02/01/2026` is January 2nd, not February 1st. This is the trap called out in `system_c.py`'s comment: reading it month-first parses days 1–12 into the wrong month silently and blows up on days 13–31 (there's no month 13). It has to be parsed day-first and then reformatted to ISO for the `Record`.\n\nSo the conversion work for `ingest` is: divide B's amount by 100, and parse C's date day-first — everything else is already in the target shape.", "ttft_ms": 7846, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 13338, "uuid": "9f147c60-e7d6-4d06-bbb6-89d0f3d56378", "ttft_stream_ms": 955, "time_to_request_ms": 150, "first_content_frame_ms": 1175, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 14.8, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "sonnet", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/P/sonnet/topic-r2-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governan